# Design Narrative
# Mechanic: Activate Champion of Dusan's Renew ability from the graveyard, exile it as a cost, and put a +1/+1 counter and a trample counter on a creature.
# Forcing: Champion is the only graveyard activation and Ironheart is the only legal creature target; two Forests provide exactly {1}{G}.
# AI behavior: The opponent has no choices, and the human starts in Main1 with every required object available.
# Failure modes:
#   WIN   = Renew resolves and updates Ironheart while Champion remains exiled.
#   LOSE  = the activation, target, payment, cost movement, or counter effect fails.
#   TIMEOUT = the activation or resolution never reaches stable priority.
# Card roles:
#   Champion of Dusan — graveyard Renew source and self-exile cost.
#   Ironheart, Clever Champion — sole creature target with a 3/4 baseline.
#   Forest — exact mana for Renew and deterministic library fillers.
# Protocol path: graveyard activation, target selection, mana payment, self-exile cost, resolution, and counter state.

[metadata]
Name:Renew - Champion of Dusan
Goal:Survive
Turns:1
Difficulty:Easy
Description:Activate Champion of Dusan from the graveyard and put its two counters on Ironheart.

